  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Southern Africa - Quarantine Pest Surveillance</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity will promote regional early warning, detection, surveillance and management of emerging pests of concern in southern Africa to safeguard agricultural productivity, thereby promoting food security and trading opportunities. The project also aims to strengthen communication between National Plant Protection Organizations in the region and enhance their surveillance and early warning systems and capabilities. Note: This activity is tentatively planned and may be delayed due to the ongoing COVID-19 situation.</narrative>
  </description>
